A. Commit message:
ASoC: Add check for negative sample_space in rz-ssi driver

B. Change summary:
Added a check to ensure that the `sample_space` is not negative before proceeding with the PIO send operation. This prevents potential issues due to type promotion of negative values to unsigned integers.

C. Compatibility Risk:
High

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/sound/soc/renesas/rz-ssi.c b/sound/soc/renesas/rz-ssi.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3a0af4ca7ab6c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sound/soc/renesas/rz-ssi.c
@@ -0,0 +1,529 @@
+/* ... (other lines of code) ... */
+
+static int rz_ssi_pio_send(struct rz_ssi_priv *ssi, struct rz_ssi_stream *strm)
+{
+	struct snd_pcm_runtime *runtime = strm->substream->runtime;
+	int frames_left = runtime->buffer_size - strm->pos;
+	int sample_space;
+	u32 ssifsr;
+
+	sample_space = strm->fifo_sample_size;
+	ssifsr = rz_ssi_reg_readl(ssi, SSIFSR);
+	sample_space -= (ssifsr >> SSIFSR_TDC_SHIFT) & SSIFSR_TDC_MASK;
+	if (sample_space < 0)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	/* Only add full frames at a time */
+	while (frames_left && (sample_space >= runtime->channels)) {
+		/* ... (rest of the function) ... */
+	}
+
+	/* ... (other lines of code) ... */
+}
+
+/* ... (other lines of code) ... */
```

